 "region": "A place with where 'region' is drawn by the region's own draw (slices/bohemia_region.js drawPlaces, through the map's mapBaseDraw by its name): its picture in place of the painted patch, the plate scaled to the patch's own blocks (a fortress 4, a camp 2) times 0.85, never under min_css (COOK SIX 11/20)",
 "sits_in_the_ground": "WORLD 15 11/26 (VAMILY rule 480(b)): bx/by/plate are where the picture's own ground plate is, measured from its pixels (tools/bohemia_world15_the_places_sit_in_the_ground_11_26_26.py; two were off: THE GREENHOUSES and THE BANK); top is its first opaque row (the tap box is the picture as drawn). slices/bohemia_place_pieces.js draws each place in depth with the painted city, so what stands in front of it is drawn over it, never under it. AND ITS LOT IS ITS BLOCK (11/26): 'wide' 1.3 and 'min_css' 46 drew a valley place's lot 1.3 blocks wide up close and 2.5 blocks wide at the map's own stop (a block 18 points), over the blocks round it: the floating look (rule 479(a): 'it reads as part of the map the way the valley's own buildings do'). Now wide 1.0 and min_css_valley 0: the lot is the block at every zoom, its edges on the streets; it reads by its own roof, its name plate and its tap. min_css stays for the region's four past the rim (COOK SIX's), which stand alone in the desert.",
